<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Bourbon</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Bourbon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Bourbon was a European royal dynasty that ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and, from the early eighteenth century, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. The Spanish Bourbons introduced administrative and fiscal reforms in the empire. Their weakness during the Napoleonic invasion of Spain helped trigger the independence movements in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-america">Spanish America</a> and the decline of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon.jpg" alt="House of Bourbon" width="286" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grand_Royal_Coat_of_Arms_of_France.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
